Infield OCR add-on
==================

The source code in this repository is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).

Release archives are different: they intentionally contain third-party binaries that are
not covered by this repository's MIT license. They are listed here and in
crates/ocr-sidecar/LICENSES/THIRD-PARTY.txt, each under its own terms:

- ONNX Runtime 1.28.0 (MIT), linked statically into the sidecar executable
  (crates/ocr-sidecar/LICENSES/onnxruntime.txt).
- DirectML.dll 1.15.4 from the Microsoft.AI.DirectML NuGet package, redistributed unmodified
  under Microsoft's DirectX Machine Learning license terms
  (crates/ocr-sidecar/LICENSES/directml.txt and directml-third-party-notices.txt).
  DirectML is not open source.
- oar-ocr 0.10.0 (Apache-2.0) and hayro 0.8.0 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT), compiled into the sidecar
  (crates/ocr-sidecar/LICENSES/oar-ocr.txt and hayro.txt).
- llama.cpp / ggml (MIT), the official ggml-org Windows Vulkan release, shipped unmodified in the
  archive's ocr-vlm/ folder, with its bundled components' licenses
  (third_party/ocr-vlm-licenses/: llama.cpp, cpp-httplib, nlohmann json, BoringSSL) and the LLVM
  OpenMP runtime (Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception).

Models are not part of this repository or of any release archive. Infield downloads them, at the
user's request, from the vendor or maintainer: the PaddleOCR-derived models (Apache-2.0) from the
oar-ocr maintainer's releases and GLM-OCR (MIT) from the llama.cpp organisation's GGUF conversion.
Their licenses apply to those files.

The exact versions, URLs, hashes and sizes of everything pinned for a release are in
config/sources.json.
